# Characters of the Mahabharata: a SKOS concept scheme
#
# Format: RDF 1.1 Turtle. Vocabulary: SKOS (https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/)
# with a small extension schema (mbhx:) for kinship and narrative relations.
# Source for the content: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahabharata and the
# character articles it links to.
# Validate with: python scripts/validate.py (SHACL shapes in shapes.ttl).
# Documentation in README.md and docs/ is generated from this file by
# scripts/render_docs.py; the specification at https://mahabharata.tanay.uk/
# (index.html) by scripts/render_site.py.
#
# Layout of this file
#   1. Prefixes and the concept scheme
#   2. Extension schema (classes and sub-properties of skos:related)
#   3. Groupings: the hierarchy that places each character
#   4. Characters, by grouping
#   5. Collections: cross-cutting groups (war sides, birth order, narrative frame)

@prefix mb:      <https://mahabharata.tanay.uk/> .
@prefix mbh:     <https://mahabharata.tanay.uk/characters#> .
@prefix mbhx:    <https://mahabharata.tanay.uk/schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix foaf:    <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix wd:      <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/> .
@prefix dbr:     <http://dbpedia.org/resource/> .
@prefix wp:      <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/> .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Concept scheme
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

mb:characters a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dcterms:title "Characters of the Mahabharata"@en ;
    dcterms:description """A SKOS concept scheme of the characters of the Mahabharata, the Sanskrit epic of the dynastic war between the Pandavas and the Kauravas for the throne of Hastinapura. Each character is a skos:Concept placed under the lineage, royal house, order or class of being the epic gives it. Collections gather characters across that hierarchy: the two sides of the war, birth order, the survivors, the narrative frame. Kinship and narrative relations between characters use sub-properties of skos:related from the companion schema. Labels are given in English, in Sanskrit in Devanagari (sa-Deva) and in IAST transliteration (sa-Latn). Epithets and patronymics are alternative labels; common spellings are hidden labels. Every character with an English Wikipedia article is mapped to its Wikidata item and DBpedia resource."""@en ;
    dcterms:created "2026-11-08"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-11-09"^^xsd:date ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ;
    dcterms:language "en", "sa" ;
    dcterms:source <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahabharata>,
                   <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_characters_in_the_Mahabharata> ;
    dcterms:conformsTo <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/> ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "The descriptions paraphrase the English Wikipedia article Mahabharata and the character articles it links to, which are published under CC BY-SA 4.0. Wikidata identifiers were resolved through the Wikipedia API on 2026-11-08."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """Modelling conventions. (1) Two kinds of concept: a mbhx:Character is a person, deity or other being; a mbhx:Grouping is a lineage, generation, royal house, order or class of being. skos:broader runs from a character to its groupings and from a grouping to a wider grouping; a character is never broader than another character. (2) A character that belongs to two groupings carries both (Draupadi is a Panchala by birth and a consort of the Pandavas by marriage; Krishna is a Yadava and the avatar of Vishnu). (3) Relations between characters are the mbhx: sub-properties of skos:related: childOf, fosterChildOf, spouseOf, siblingOf, studentOf, killedBy, charioteerOf, rebirthOf, avatarOf, friendOf, rivalOf, cursed. Each relation is stated once, in the direction the property names; the inverse is declared in the schema. siblingOf is stated only where the shared parent is not a concept in this scheme. (4) skos:Collection groups characters across the hierarchy; skos:OrderedCollection is used where the order carries meaning. (5) skos:exactMatch points to Wikidata and DBpedia; skos:closeMatch is used where the external resource is wider than the concept (a kingdom for a royal house, Yama for Dharma). foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf points to the English Wikipedia article."""@en ;
    foaf:homepage <https://mahabharata.tanay.uk/> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Every IRI of the scheme resolves to its entry in the specification at https://mahabharata.tanay.uk/: the fragment of a concept IRI (https://mahabharata.tanay.uk/characters#arjuna) or of a schema IRI (https://mahabharata.tanay.uk/schema#childOf) is the anchor of its description there. To publish under another namespace, edit the mb:, mbh: and mbhx: prefix declarations in this file and in shapes.ttl, and the namespace constants at the top of the scripts. The scheme covers the characters named in the Wikipedia synopsis and the principal figures of the Kurukshetra war. The epic names many hundreds more."@en ;
    skos:hasTopConcept mbh:house-of-kuru, mbh:yadavas, mbh:panchala, mbh:other-royal-houses,
                       mbh:brahmins-and-sages, mbh:sutas, mbh:deities, mbh:other-beings .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Extension schema
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

mb:schema a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:title "Characters of the Mahabharata: SKOS extension schema"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ;
    rdfs:comment "Two subclasses of skos:Concept that separate characters from the groupings that organise them, one datatype property, and sub-properties of skos:related for kinship and narrative relations. SKOS allows such specialisation (SKOS Primer, section 4.7): a sub-property of skos:related inherits its meaning and stays within SKOS semantics. skos:related is symmetric, but that places no restriction on its sub-properties (SKOS Reference, section 8.6.3), so each sub-property here either has a declared inverse or is itself declared symmetric."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/#semantic-relations>, <https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-primer/#secskosspecialization> .

mbhx:Character a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Character"@en ;
    skos:definition "A person, deity or other being that acts or is named in the Mahabharata."@en .

mbhx:Grouping a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    owl:disjointWith mbhx:Character ;
    rdfs:label "Grouping"@en ;
    skos:definition "A lineage, generation, royal house, order or class of being under which characters are placed in the hierarchy."@en .

mbhx:fellOnWarDay a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "fell on war day"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mbhx:Character ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    skos:definition "The day of the eighteen-day Kurukshetra war on which the character was struck down. Bhishma falls on day 10 and dies after the war; the night raid after day 18 is counted as day 18."@en .

mbhx:characterRelation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf skos:related ;
    rdfs:label "character relation"@en ;
    rdfs:domain mbhx:Character ;
    rdfs:range mbhx:Character ;
    skos:definition "Parent of every relation between two characters in this scheme. Not used directly."@en .

mbhx:childOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:parentOf ;
    rdfs:label "child of"@en ;
    skos:definition "The subject is a child of the object, as the epic states parentage."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Covers birth, fathering by a deity through Kunti's boon (the Pandavas, Karna) and fatherhood by niyoga (Dhritarashtra, Pandu and Vidura as sons of Vichitravirya; the Pandavas as sons of Pandu). The notes on the characters say which applies."@en .

mbhx:parentOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:childOf ;
    rdfs:label "parent of"@en .

mbhx:fosterChildOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:fosterParentOf ;
    rdfs:label "foster child of"@en ;
    skos:definition "The subject was raised by the object without being born to them."@en .

mbhx:fosterParentOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:fosterChildOf ;
    rdfs:label "foster parent of"@en .

mbhx:spouseOf a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    rdfs:label "spouse of"@en ;
    skos:definition "The subject and the object are married."@en .

mbhx:siblingOf a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    rdfs:label "sibling of"@en ;
    skos:definition "The subject and the object share a parent."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Stated only where the shared parent is not a concept in this scheme; otherwise the relation follows from childOf."@en .

mbhx:studentOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:teacherOf ;
    rdfs:label "student of"@en ;
    skos:definition "The object taught the subject, in arms or in learning."@en .

mbhx:teacherOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:studentOf ;
    rdfs:label "teacher of"@en .

mbhx:killedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:killed ;
    rdfs:label "killed by"@en ;
    skos:definition "The object struck the blow that killed the subject, or in Bhishma's case the blow that brought him down."@en .

mbhx:killed a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:killedBy ;
    rdfs:label "killed"@en .

mbhx:charioteerOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:hasCharioteer ;
    rdfs:label "charioteer of"@en ;
    skos:definition "The subject drove the object's chariot."@en .

mbhx:hasCharioteer a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:charioteerOf ;
    rdfs:label "has charioteer"@en .

mbhx:rebirthOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:rebornAs ;
    rdfs:label "rebirth of"@en ;
    skos:definition "The subject is the object born again in a later life."@en .

mbhx:rebornAs a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:rebirthOf ;
    rdfs:label "reborn as"@en .

mbhx:avatarOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:hasAvatar ;
    rdfs:label "avatar of"@en ;
    skos:definition "The subject is an incarnation of the deity named by the object."@en .

mbhx:hasAvatar a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:avatarOf ;
    rdfs:label "has avatar"@en .

mbhx:friendOf a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    rdfs:label "friend of"@en ;
    skos:definition "A friendship the epic treats as a defining bond."@en .

mbhx:rivalOf a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    rdfs:label "rival of"@en ;
    skos:definition "A personal enmity the epic treats as a defining bond."@en .

mbhx:cursed a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:cursedBy ;
    rdfs:label "cursed"@en ;
    skos:definition "The subject pronounced a curse on the object that takes effect in the story."@en .

mbhx:cursedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf mbhx:characterRelation ;
    owl:inverseOf mbhx:cursed ;
    rdfs:label "cursed by"@en .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Groupings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

mbh:house-of-kuru a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:topConceptOf mb:characters ;
    skos:prefLabel "House of Kuru"@en, "कुरुवंश"@sa-Deva, "Kuruvaṁśa"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Kuru dynasty"@en, "Kurus"@en ;
    skos:definition "The royal lineage of Hastinapura descended from King Kuru, to which both the Pandavas and the Kauravas belong."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Arranged by generation, from Shantanu to Janamejaya. Women who marry into the house are placed in the generation of their husbands. The word Kaurava in its narrow sense means the sons of Dhritarashtra; see the Kauravas grouping."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q1068408, dbr:Kuru_kingdom ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Kuru_kingdom .

mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:house-of-kuru ;
    skos:prefLabel "House of Kuru: generation of Shantanu"@en ;
    skos:definition "Shantanu, his brother Bahlika, his queen Satyavati, his sons Bhishma, Chitrangada and Vichitravirya, and Vichitravirya's wives Ambika and Ambalika."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Shantanu's first wife Ganga is placed under Deities and linked to him by spouseOf."@en .

mbh:kuru-generation-pandu a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:house-of-kuru ;
    skos:prefLabel "House of Kuru: generation of Pandu"@en ;
    skos:definition "The sons born to Vichitravirya's widows by Vyasa, and their wives: Dhritarashtra and Gandhari, Pandu with Kunti and Madri, and Vidura."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Gandhari, Kunti and Madri are also placed under the houses of their birth."@en .

mbh:pandavas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:house-of-kuru ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pandavas"@en, "पाण्डव"@sa-Deva, "Pāṇḍava"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Sons of Pandu"@en, "Pandava brothers"@en ;
    skos:definition "The five sons of Pandu, born to Kunti and Madri through the gods Kunti invoked, and the protagonists of the epic."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Only the five brothers. Their wives are under Consorts of the Pandavas and their sons under Children of the Pandavas."@en ;
    skos:related mbh:kauravas ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q236221, dbr:Pandava ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Pandava .

mbh:kauravas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:house-of-kuru ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kauravas"@en, "कौरव"@sa-Deva, "Kaurava"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Sons of Dhritarashtra"@en, "Dhartarashtras"@en ;
    skos:definition "The hundred sons of Dhritarashtra and Gandhari, led by Duryodhana, together with their sister Dussala and their half-brother Yuyutsu."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Used in the narrow sense of the children of Dhritarashtra. In the broad sense Kaurava means any descendant of Kuru, which includes the Pandavas. Only the children with a part of their own in the story are listed."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1648561, dbr:Kaurava ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Kaurava .

mbh:consorts-of-the-pandavas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:house-of-kuru ;
    skos:prefLabel "Consorts of the Pandavas"@en ;
    skos:definition "Women married to one or more of the five Pandavas: Draupadi, the wife of all five, and the wives of Bhima and Arjuna whose sons fight in the war."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Draupadi, Hidimbi, Ulupi, Chitrangada of Manipura and Subhadra. Wives who take no part in the story are not listed. Each consort is also placed under her house or people of birth."@en .

mbh:children-of-the-pandavas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:house-of-kuru ;
    skos:prefLabel "Children of the Pandavas"@en ;
    skos:definition "The sons of the five Pandavas who act in the epic: the five sons of Draupadi, and the sons of Arjuna and Bhima by their other wives."@en .

mbh:upapandavas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:children-of-the-pandavas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Upapandavas"@en, "उपपाण्डव"@sa-Deva, "Upapāṇḍava"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Draupadeyas"@en, "Sons of Draupadi"@en, "द्रौपदेय"@sa-Deva, "Draupadeya"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "The five sons of Draupadi, one by each Pandava, all killed in their sleep by Ashwatthama on the night after the last day of the war."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q7898172, dbr:Draupadeyas ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Draupadeyas .

mbh:children-of-the-kauravas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:house-of-kuru ;
    skos:prefLabel "Children of the Kauravas"@en ;
    skos:definition "Sons of Dhritarashtra's sons who act in the epic: Lakshmana Kumara, Duryodhana's son, and Durmasena, Dushasana's son, both of whom fall in the fight around Abhimanyu."@en .

mbh:later-kuru-kings a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:house-of-kuru ;
    skos:prefLabel "House of Kuru: kings after the war"@en ;
    skos:definition "The Kuru kings of Hastinapura after Yudhishthira: Parikshit and his son Janamejaya, at whose snake sacrifice the epic is recited."@en .

mbh:yadavas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:topConceptOf mb:characters ;
    skos:prefLabel "Yadavas"@en, "यादव"@sa-Deva, "Yādava"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Vrishnis"@en, "Yadus"@en ;
    skos:definition "The clan of Krishna, descended from Yadu, including the Vrishni, Andhaka and Bhoja branches, with their capital at Dwaraka."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kunti belongs here by birth as the daughter of the Yadava Shurasena, and Kuntibhoja as Shurasena's cousin."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q8046532, dbr:Yadava ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Yadava .

mbh:panchala a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:topConceptOf mb:characters ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Panchala"@en, "पाञ्चाल"@sa-Deva, "Pāñcāla"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Panchalas"@en ;
    skos:definition "The royal family of the Panchala kingdom under Drupada, allied by marriage to the Pandavas through Draupadi."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q558603, dbr:Panchala ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Panchala .

mbh:other-royal-houses a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:topConceptOf mb:characters ;
    skos:prefLabel "Other royal houses"@en ;
    skos:definition "Royal families of kingdoms other than Kuru, Yadava and Panchala whose members act in the epic, grouped by kingdom."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "A kingdom appears here only if one of its royal family is a character in the scheme."@en .

mbh:kingdom-matsya a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Matsya"@en, "मत्स्य"@sa-Deva, "Matsya"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "The family of King Virata, at whose court the Pandavas spend the thirteenth year of their exile in disguise."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q113100727 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matsya_(kingdom)> .

mbh:kingdom-madra a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Madra"@en, "मद्र"@sa-Deva, "Madra"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "The family of Shalya: his sister Madri marries Pandu, and Shalya fights for the Kauravas."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q6728459, dbr:Madra_kingdom ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Madra_kingdom .

mbh:kingdom-gandhara a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Gandhara"@en, "गान्धार"@sa-Deva, "Gāndhāra"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "The children of King Subala: Gandhari, who marries Dhritarashtra, and Shakuni, who engineers the dice game, with Shakuni's son Uluka."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q112980583 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gandhāra_Kingdom> .

mbh:kingdom-anga a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Anga"@en, "अङ्ग"@sa-Deva, "Aṅga"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Karna, whom Duryodhana crowns king of Anga, and his son Vrishasena."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q1155818, dbr:Anga ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Anga .

mbh:kingdom-kashi a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Kashi"@en, "काशी"@sa-Deva, "Kāśī"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "The three princesses of Kashi whom Bhishma carries off from their swayamvara: Amba, Ambika and Ambalika."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q12660335 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kāśī_(kingdom)> .

mbh:kingdom-sindhu a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Sindhu"@en, "सिन्धु"@sa-Deva, "Sindhu"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Jayadratha, king of Sindhu and husband of Dussala."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q7522239, dbr:Sindhu_Kingdom ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Sindhu_Kingdom .

mbh:kingdom-magadha a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Magadha"@en, "मगध"@sa-Deva, "Magadha"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Jarasandha, the king of Magadha whom Bhima kills before Yudhishthira's royal consecration."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q234009, dbr:Magadha ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Magadha .

mbh:kingdom-chedi a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Chedi"@en, "चेदि"@sa-Deva, "Cedi"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Shishupala, whom Krishna kills at the royal consecration, and his son Dhrishtaketu, who fights for the Pandavas."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q1329944, dbr:Chedi_kingdom ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Chedi_kingdom .

mbh:kingdom-pragjyotisha a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Pragjyotisha"@en, "प्राग्ज्योतिष"@sa-Deva, "Prāgjyotiṣa"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Bhagadatta, the elephant-riding king of Pragjyotisha who fights for the Kauravas."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q1194765 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Kamarupa .

mbh:kingdom-trigarta a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Trigarta"@en, "त्रिगर्त"@sa-Deva, "Trigarta"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Susharma, king of Trigarta and leader of the Samsaptakas, who fights for the Kauravas."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q7841669, dbr:Trigarta ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Trigarta .

mbh:kingdom-kamboja a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Kamboja"@en, "कम्बोज"@sa-Deva, "Kamboja"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Sudakshina, king of the Kambojas, who fights for the Kauravas."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q6356381, dbr:Kamboja ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Kamboja .

mbh:kingdom-bahlika a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Bahlika"@en, "बाह्लीक"@sa-Deva, "Bāhlīka"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "The Kuru branch that rules Bahlika: Shantanu's brother Bahlika, his son Somadatta and his grandson Bhurishravas, all of whom fight for the Kauravas."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q4272177, dbr:Bahlikas ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Bahlikas .

mbh:kingdom-nishada a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of the Nishadas"@en, "निषाद"@sa-Deva, "Niṣāda"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Ekalavya, the Nishada prince who teaches himself archery."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q7040266, dbr:Nishadas ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Nishadas .

mbh:kingdom-vidarbha a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Vidarbha"@en, "विदर्भ"@sa-Deva, "Vidarbha"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Rukmi, king of Vidarbha and brother of Krishna's wife Rukmini."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q7927728, dbr:Vidarbha_kingdom ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Vidarbha_kingdom .

mbh:kingdom-manipura a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-royal-houses ;
    skos:prefLabel "Royal house of Manipura"@en, "मणिपुर"@sa-Deva, "Maṇipura"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Chitrangada, who marries Arjuna, and their son Babruvahana, who rules Manipura after his grandfather."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q106452195 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manipura_(Mahabharata)> .

mbh:brahmins-and-sages a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:topConceptOf mb:characters ;
    skos:prefLabel "Brahmins and sages"@en ;
    skos:definition "Brahmin characters: the sages who compose, narrate and intervene in the story, and the Brahmin warriors who teach arms to the Kuru princes."@en .

mbh:sages a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:brahmins-and-sages ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sages"@en, "ऋषि"@sa-Deva, "Ṛṣi"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Rishis"@en ;
    skos:definition "Seers and ascetics who compose, narrate and shape the story through boons and curses."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q755990, dbr:Rishi ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Rishi .

mbh:warrior-brahmins a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:brahmins-and-sages ;
    skos:prefLabel "Brahmin warriors of the Kuru court"@en ;
    skos:definition "Drona's family and Kripa: Brahmins by birth who teach arms to the Kuru princes and fight for the Kauravas."@en .

mbh:sutas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:topConceptOf mb:characters ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sutas"@en, "सूत"@sa-Deva, "Sūta"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Charioteers and bards"@en ;
    skos:definition "Members of the suta class of charioteers and bards: the epic's reciter Ugrashravas, Dhritarashtra's narrator Sanjaya, and Karna's foster family."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Karna is placed here as the son of a suta household and under Anga as its king."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q7649873, dbr:Suta ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Suta .

mbh:deities a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:topConceptOf mb:characters ;
    skos:prefLabel "Deities and celestial beings"@en, "देव"@sa-Deva, "Deva"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Gods"@en ;
    skos:definition "Gods, goddesses and celestial beings who father, marry, test, arm or curse the human characters."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Krishna is placed here as the avatar of Vishnu and under the Yadavas by birth. Hanuman and the nymph Urvashi are included as celestial beings."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q211258 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deva_(Hinduism)> .

mbh:other-beings a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:topConceptOf mb:characters ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rakshasas, Nagas and Asuras"@en ;
    skos:definition "Non-human peoples of the epic other than the gods: the rakshasas the Pandavas fight and marry, the serpent Nagas, and the asura architect Maya."@en .

mbh:rakshasas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-beings ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rakshasas"@en, "राक्षस"@sa-Deva, "Rākṣasa"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Man-eating forest beings, several of whom Bhima kills, and the family into which he marries."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q1049467, dbr:Rakshasa ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Rakshasa .

mbh:nagas a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-beings ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nagas"@en, "नाग"@sa-Deva, "Nāga"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Serpent beings: Arjuna's wife Ulupi and the serpent king Takshaka, whose bite kills Parikshit."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q271990, dbr:Nāga ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Nāga .

mbh:asuras a mbhx:Grouping, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:other-beings ;
    skos:prefLabel "Asuras and Danavas"@en, "असुर"@sa-Deva, "Asura"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Demons; in this scheme the Danava architect Maya."@en ;
    skos:closeMatch wd:Q624083, dbr:Asura ;
    rdfs:seeAlso wp:Asura .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Characters
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 4.1 House of Kuru: generation of Shantanu

mbh:shantanu a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu ;
    skos:prefLabel "Shantanu"@en, "शान्तनु"@sa-Deva, "Śāntanu"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Santanu"@en, "Shantanu of Hastinapura"@en ;
    skos:definition "King of Hastinapura, husband of the goddess Ganga and then of the fisherwoman Satyavati, and father of Bhishma, Chitrangada and Vichitravirya."@en ;
    skos:note "Satyavati's father agreed to the marriage only on the promise that her son would inherit the throne. Devavrata, later Bhishma, gave up his claim and vowed lifelong celibacy to secure it."@en ;
    mbhx:spouseOf mbh:ganga, mbh:satyavati ;
    mbhx:siblingOf mbh:bahlika ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1973947, dbr:Shantanu ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Shantanu .

mbh:bahlika a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu, mbh:kingdom-bahlika ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bahlika"@en, "बाह्लीक"@sa-Deva, "Bāhlīka"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Vahlika"@en, "Balhika"@en ;
    skos:definition "Elder brother of Shantanu who left Hastinapura to rule the Bahlika kingdom; the oldest warrior on the field at Kurukshetra, where he fights for the Kauravas and is killed by Bhima."@en ;
    mbhx:killedBy mbh:bhima ;
    mbhx:fellOnWarDay 14 ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q12452536, <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bahlika_(king)> ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bahlika_(king)> .

mbh:satyavati a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu ;
    skos:prefLabel "Satyavati"@en, "सत्यवती"@sa-Deva, "Satyavatī"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Matsyagandha"@en, "Yojanagandha"@en, "Daseyi"@en, "मत्स्यगन्धा"@sa-Deva, "Matsyagandhā"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Satyawati"@en ;
    skos:definition "Daughter of the chief of the fishermen, mother of Vyasa by the sage Parashara before her marriage, queen of Shantanu, and mother of Chitrangada and Vichitravirya."@en ;
    skos:note "When Vichitravirya died childless she called on Vyasa to father children with his widows, which produced Dhritarashtra, Pandu and Vidura."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q2044655, dbr:Satyavati ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Satyavati .

mbh:bhishma a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bhishma"@en, "भीष्म"@sa-Deva, "Bhīṣma"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Devavrata"@en, "Gangaputra"@en, "Gangeya"@en, "Shantanava"@en, "Pitamaha"@en, "देवव्रत"@sa-Deva, "Devavrata"@sa-Latn, "Gāṅgeya"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Bhishm"@en, "Bheeshma"@en ;
    skos:definition "Son of Shantanu and Ganga, born Devavrata; the Kuru patriarch who renounced the throne and vowed celibacy so that Satyavati's son could inherit, and who commands the Kaurava army for the first ten days of the war."@en ;
    skos:note "He carried off the three princesses of Kashi for Vichitravirya, which made Amba his lifelong enemy. He held a boon to choose the hour of his death. Felled by Arjuna's arrows on day 10 while refusing to fight Shikhandi, he lay on a bed of arrows until the sun's northward turn, instructing Yudhishthira in the duties of a king before he died."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:shantanu, mbh:ganga ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:parashurama ;
    mbhx:killedBy mbh:arjuna ;
    mbhx:fellOnWarDay 10 ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1405629, dbr:Bhishma ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Bhishma .

mbh:chitrangada-kuru a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu ;
    skos:prefLabel "Chitrangada (son of Shantanu)"@en, "चित्राङ्गद"@sa-Deva, "Citrāṅgada"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Chitrangad"@en ;
    skos:definition "Elder son of Shantanu and Satyavati, who succeeded his father and was killed in a long duel by a gandharva of the same name."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Not the princess of Manipura who marries Arjuna; see Chitrangada (princess of Manipura)."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:shantanu, mbh:satyavati ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1994800, <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chitrangada_(king)> ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chitrangada_(king)> .

mbh:vichitravirya a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu ;
    skos:prefLabel "Vichitravirya"@en, "विचित्रवीर्य"@sa-Deva, "Vicitravīrya"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Vichitraveerya"@en ;
    skos:definition "Younger son of Shantanu and Satyavati, king of Hastinapura after Chitrangada, married to Ambika and Ambalika, who died childless."@en ;
    skos:note "By the custom of niyoga, the sons Vyasa fathered with his widows, Dhritarashtra and Pandu, and with their maid, Vidura, count as his."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:shantanu, mbh:satyavati ;
    mbhx:spouseOf mbh:ambika, mbh:ambalika ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1987279, dbr:Vichitravirya ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Vichitravirya .

mbh:ambika a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu, mbh:kingdom-kashi ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ambika"@en, "अम्बिका"@sa-Deva, "Ambikā"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Princess of Kashi and wife of Vichitravirya; she shut her eyes before Vyasa during the niyoga, and her son Dhritarashtra was born blind."@en ;
    mbhx:siblingOf mbh:amba, mbh:ambalika ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q2044636, <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ambika_(Mahabharata)> ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambika_(Mahabharata)> .

mbh:ambalika a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-shantanu, mbh:kingdom-kashi ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ambalika"@en, "अम्बालिका"@sa-Deva, "Ambālikā"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Princess of Kashi and wife of Vichitravirya; she turned pale before Vyasa during the niyoga, and her son Pandu was born pale."@en ;
    mbhx:siblingOf mbh:amba ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1994807, dbr:Ambalika ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Ambalika .

# 4.2 House of Kuru: generation of Pandu

mbh:dhritarashtra a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-pandu ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dhritarashtra"@en, "धृतराष्ट्र"@sa-Deva, "Dhṛtarāṣṭra"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Dhritrashtra"@en, "Dhritarastra"@en ;
    skos:definition "Blind king of Hastinapura, son of Vyasa and Ambika, husband of Gandhari and father of the hundred Kauravas; the war is narrated to him by Sanjaya."@en ;
    skos:note "Passed over for the throne because of his blindness, he ruled after Pandu's death. He could not restrain Duryodhana. After the war he retired to the forest with Gandhari and Kunti, where all three died in a forest fire."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:vyasa, mbh:ambika, mbh:vichitravirya ;
    mbhx:spouseOf mbh:gandhari ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q926150, dbr:Dhritarashtra ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Dhritarashtra .

mbh:gandhari a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-pandu, mbh:kingdom-gandhara ;
    skos:prefLabel "Gandhari"@en, "गान्धारी"@sa-Deva, "Gāndhārī"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Saubaleyi"@en ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Gandhaari"@en ;
    skos:definition "Princess of Gandhara, sister of Shakuni and wife of Dhritarashtra, who blindfolded herself for life to share her husband's blindness; mother of the hundred Kauravas and of Dussala."@en ;
    skos:note "After the war she cursed Krishna: his own clan would destroy itself as hers had. The curse was fulfilled thirty-six years later."@en ;
    mbhx:siblingOf mbh:shakuni ;
    mbhx:cursed mbh:krishna ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1849082, dbr:Gandhari ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Gandhari .

mbh:pandu a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-pandu ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pandu"@en, "पाण्डु"@sa-Deva, "Pāṇḍu"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Pandu of Hastinapura"@en ;
    skos:definition "Son of Vyasa and Ambalika, king of Hastinapura before Dhritarashtra, husband of Kunti and Madri, and father of the five Pandavas."@en ;
    skos:note "Cursed by the sage Kindama, whom he shot while the sage was in the form of a deer, to die if he ever lay with a woman, he withdrew to the forest. His sons were born through the gods Kunti invoked and count as his by niyoga. He died embracing Madri."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:vyasa, mbh:ambalika, mbh:vichitravirya ;
    mbhx:spouseOf mbh:kunti, mbh:madri ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q857071, dbr:Pandu ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Pandu .

mbh:kunti a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-pandu, mbh:yadavas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kunti"@en, "कुन्ती"@sa-Deva, "Kuntī"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Pritha"@en, "पृथा"@sa-Deva, "Pṛthā"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Kunthi"@en ;
    skos:definition "Daughter of the Yadava Shurasena, raised by Kuntibhoja; first wife of Pandu and mother of Karna by Surya before her marriage, and of Yudhishthira, Bhima and Arjuna by the gods Dharma, Vayu and Indra."@en ;
    skos:note "The sage Durvasa gave her a mantra to summon any god for a son. She shared it with Madri. She raised the five brothers after Pandu's death and died in the forest fire with Dhritarashtra and Gandhari."@en ;
    mbhx:fosterChildOf mbh:kuntibhoja ;
    mbhx:siblingOf mbh:vasudeva ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:durvasa ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q844424, dbr:Kunti ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Kunti .

mbh:madri a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-pandu, mbh:kingdom-madra ;
    skos:prefLabel "Madri"@en, "माद्री"@sa-Deva, "Mādrī"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Maadri"@en ;
    skos:definition "Princess of Madra, sister of Shalya and second wife of Pandu; mother of the twins Nakula and Sahadeva by the Ashvins."@en ;
    skos:note "Pandu died in her arms, breaking Kindama's curse; she followed him onto the pyre and left the twins to Kunti."@en ;
    mbhx:siblingOf mbh:shalya ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1770690, dbr:Madri ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Madri .

mbh:vidura a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kuru-generation-pandu ;
    skos:prefLabel "Vidura"@en, "विदुर"@sa-Deva, "Vidura"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Kshatta"@en ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Vidur"@en ;
    skos:definition "Son of Vyasa and a maid of the Kashi princesses, half-brother of Dhritarashtra and Pandu, and chief minister of Hastinapura, held to be the wisest man of the epic and an incarnation of the god Dharma."@en ;
    skos:note "He warned the Pandavas of the house of lac and sent the miner who dug their escape tunnel. He protested the dice game and the treatment of Draupadi. He did not fight in the war."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:vyasa, mbh:vichitravirya ;
    mbhx:avatarOf mbh:dharma ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q2002511, dbr:Vidura ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Vidura .

# 4.3 Pandavas

mbh:yudhishthira a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:pandavas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Yudhishthira"@en, "युधिष्ठिर"@sa-Deva, "Yudhiṣṭhira"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Dharmaraja"@en, "Ajatashatru"@en, "Dharmaputra"@en, "Kanka"@en, "धर्मराज"@sa-Deva, "Dharmarāja"@sa-Latn, "Ajātaśatru"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Yudhisthira"@en, "Yudhishthir"@en, "Yudhisthir"@en, "Dharmaraj"@en ;
    skos:definition "Eldest Pandava, son of Kunti and the god Dharma, known for his truthfulness; he loses the kingdom at dice, leads his brothers through exile and war, and rules Hastinapura after the victory."@en ;
    skos:note "His royal consecration provoked Duryodhana's envy. He answered the questions of the Yaksha at the lake during the exile. At Virata's court he served as the courtier Kanka. He killed Shalya on day 18. On the final journey he alone reached heaven in the body, with a dog who was Dharma in disguise."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:kunti, mbh:pandu, mbh:dharma ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:drona, mbh:bhishma ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q983067, dbr:Yudhishthira ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Yudhishthira .

mbh:bhima a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:pandavas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bhima"@en, "भीम"@sa-Deva, "Bhīma"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Bhimasena"@en, "Vrikodara"@en, "Vallabha"@en, "भीमसेन"@sa-Deva, "Bhīmasena"@sa-Latn, "Vṛkodara"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Bheem"@en, "Bhim"@en, "Bheema"@en ;
    skos:definition "Second Pandava, son of Kunti and the wind god Vayu, the strongest of the brothers and a mace fighter; he kills Hidimba, Bakasura, Kirmira, Jarasandha, Kichaka and, in the war, Dushasana and Duryodhana."@en ;
    skos:note "He vowed to drink Dushasana's blood and to break Duryodhana's thigh for the humiliation of Draupadi, and did both. At Virata's court he served as the cook Vallabha. Hanuman, also a son of Vayu, is his brother."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:kunti, mbh:pandu, mbh:vayu ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:drona, mbh:balarama ;
    mbhx:rivalOf mbh:duryodhana ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q3651886, dbr:Bhima ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Bhima .

mbh:arjuna a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:pandavas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Arjuna"@en, "अर्जुन"@sa-Deva, "Arjuna"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Partha"@en, "Dhananjaya"@en, "Savyasachi"@en, "Phalguna"@en, "Kiriti"@en, "Bibhatsu"@en, "Jishnu"@en, "Vijaya"@en, "Shvetavahana"@en, "Gudakesha"@en, "Brihannala"@en, "पार्थ"@sa-Deva, "धनञ्जय"@sa-Deva, "Pārtha"@sa-Latn, "Dhanañjaya"@sa-Latn, "Savyasācin"@sa-Latn, "Bṛhannalā"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Arjun"@en, "Arjunan"@en ;
    skos:definition "Third Pandava, son of Kunti and Indra, the greatest archer of the epic, Krishna's friend and brother-in-law, and the hearer of the Bhagavad Gita."@en ;
    skos:note "He won Draupadi at her swayamvara. He married Ulupi, Chitrangada and Subhadra during and after his year of pilgrimage. His bow Gandiva came from Agni at the burning of the Khandava forest. He spent the thirteenth year of exile as the dance teacher Brihannala. In the war he brought down Bhishma, killed Jayadratha, Bhagadatta, Sudakshina, Bhurishravas (disarmed), Vrishasena, Karna and Susharma, with Krishna as his charioteer. His flag carried Hanuman."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:kunti, mbh:pandu, mbh:indra ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:drona ;
    mbhx:friendOf mbh:krishna ;
    mbhx:rivalOf mbh:karna ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q185790, dbr:Arjuna ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Arjuna .

mbh:nakula a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:pandavas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nakula"@en, "नकुल"@sa-Deva, "Nakula"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Granthika"@en ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Nakul"@en ;
    skos:definition "Fourth Pandava, elder twin son of Madri and the Ashvins, famed for his beauty, horsemanship and swordsmanship."@en ;
    skos:note "At Virata's court he served as the horse keeper Granthika. He fought Karna on day 17 and was spared because of Karna's promise to Kunti."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:madri, mbh:pandu, mbh:ashvins ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:drona ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1978476, dbr:Nakula ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Nakula .

mbh:sahadeva a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:pandavas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sahadeva"@en, "सहदेव"@sa-Deva, "Sahadeva"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Tantipala"@en ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Sahadev"@en ;
    skos:definition "Youngest Pandava, twin son of Madri and the Ashvins, learned in astrology and the scriptures; he kills Shakuni and Uluka on the last day of the war."@en ;
    skos:note "At Virata's court he served as the cowherd Tantipala. He had vowed to kill Shakuni for the dice game."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:madri, mbh:pandu, mbh:ashvins ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:drona ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q2044641, dbr:Sahadeva ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Sahadeva .

# 4.4 Kauravas

mbh:duryodhana a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kauravas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Duryodhana"@en, "दुर्योधन"@sa-Deva, "Duryodhana"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:altLabel "Suyodhana"@en, "सुयोधन"@sa-Deva, "Suyodhana"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Duryodhan"@en, "Duryodhanan"@en ;
    skos:definition "Eldest of the hundred Kauravas, son of Dhritarashtra and Gandhari, the Pandavas' rival from childhood who refuses to share the kingdom and leads the Kaurava side in the war."@en ;
    skos:note "Humiliated at Yudhishthira's palace at Indraprastha, he staged the dice game on Shakuni's advice. He made Karna king of Anga and kept him as his closest friend. Bhima broke his thighs in the final mace duel on day 18, as he had vowed."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:dhritarashtra, mbh:gandhari ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:drona, mbh:balarama ;
    mbhx:friendOf mbh:karna ;
    mbhx:killedBy mbh:bhima ;
    mbhx:fellOnWarDay 18 ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q1405823, dbr:Duryodhana ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Duryodhana .

mbh:dushasana a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kauravas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dushasana"@en, "दुःशासन"@sa-Deva, "Duḥśāsana"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Duhshasana"@en, "Dusshasana"@en, "Dushasan"@en ;
    skos:definition "Second of the Kauravas, who dragged Draupadi by the hair into the assembly after the dice game and tried to strip her; Bhima kills him on day 17 and drinks his blood as he had vowed."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:dhritarashtra, mbh:gandhari ;
    mbhx:studentOf mbh:drona ;
    mbhx:killedBy mbh:bhima ;
    mbhx:fellOnWarDay 17 ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q2044646, dbr:Duhshasana ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Duhshasana .

mbh:vikarna a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kauravas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Vikarna"@en, "विकर्ण"@sa-Deva, "Vikarṇa"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "A Kaurava who alone among his brothers spoke against the staking and humiliation of Draupadi at the dice game, and who still fought for Duryodhana; Bhima kills him with regret."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:dhritarashtra, mbh:gandhari ;
    mbhx:killedBy mbh:bhima ;
    mbhx:fellOnWarDay 14 ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q7929388, dbr:Vikarna ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Vikarna .

mbh:yuyutsu a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kauravas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Yuyutsu"@en, "युयुत्सु"@sa-Deva, "Yuyutsu"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:definition "Son of Dhritarashtra by a Vaishya woman of the household, and so half-brother of the Kauravas; he crossed to the Pandava side when the armies were drawn up and survived the war."@en ;
    skos:note "After the war Yudhishthira left him as a guardian of Hastinapura for Parikshit."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:dhritarashtra ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q2392426, dbr:Yuyutsu ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Yuyutsu .

mbh:dussala a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:kauravas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dussala"@en, "दुःशला"@sa-Deva, "Duḥśalā"@sa-Latn ;
    skos:hiddenLabel "Duhshala"@en, "Dushala"@en, "Duhsala"@en ;
    skos:definition "Only daughter of Dhritarashtra and Gandhari, wife of Jayadratha of Sindhu."@en ;
    mbhx:childOf mbh:dhritarashtra, mbh:gandhari ;
    skos:exactMatch wd:Q2723039, dbr:Duhshala ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf wp:Duhshala .

# 4.5 Children of the Kauravas

mbh:lakshmana-kumara a mbhx:Character, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme mb:characters ;
    skos:broader mbh:children-of-the-kauravas ;
    skos:prefLabel "Lakshmana Kumara"@en, "लक्ष्मण कुमार"@sa-Deva, "Lakṣmaṇa Kumāra"@sa-Latn ;
